# LEGIT OS offensive security tools
# One package per line. Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# IMPORTANT: only packages available in the official Arch repositories are
# listed here. Tools requiring the AUR are intentionally NOT enabled (the
# project does not ship a personal Pacman repository); they are documented in
# the commented section at the bottom for deliberate, conscious additions.

# --- RECON / SCAN ---
nmap
masscan
rustscan
arp-scan
macchanger
tcpdump
traceroute
openbsd-netcat
socat
proxychains-ng
openvpn

# --- WEB / APP TESTING ---
sqlmap
nikto
gobuster
zaproxy

# --- EXPLOIT / FRAMEWORKS ---
metasploit
exploitdb

# --- BRUTE FORCE / PASSWORD ---
hydra
medusa
john
hashcat

# --- WIRELESS ---
aircrack-ng
wireless_tools

# --- SNIFFING / MITM ---
wireshark-qt
wireshark-cli
bettercap
mitmproxy

# --- REVERSE ENGINEERING / BINARY ---
radare2
rizin
ghidra
gdb
yara
binwalk
strace

# --- SUPPORT / MISC ---
binutils
python-pwntools
python-requests
samba
freerdp

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not packaged in official repositories (AUR only) - NOT installed.
# Removed from the enabled list: dirb, dirsearch, gnu-netcat, netdiscover,
# tshark (wireshark-cli provides it), wafw00f, whatweb.
# Manual candidates if a maintainer ever makes them explicit:
#   burpsuite, bloodhound, evilginx2, getsploit, msfvenom-wrappers, scylla
